file = "rpc/state.go:150-176"
symbol = "GetProof"
observed = "Attempt 1 (325c5464b) builds, writes the vector and verifies the committed two-op proof against the stored app hash; the test then fails at names_proof_test.go:217 because the live eth_getProof answer does not verify against the commit hash (calculated root hash is invalid). GetProof queries the evm KV store itself (findQueryableKVStore, path /key), so each StorageProof carries only the ics23:iavl op from key to the evm store root and never the ics23:simple op from the store root to the app hash; the root multistore query at /evm/key yields both ops. The previous attempt declared rpc/state.go out of scope."
assumption = "Acceptance 19003.1 requires the eth_getProof answer itself to verify against the app hash, so GetProof queries the root multistore (decision 2173); rpc/state.go, rpc/server.go and the test files that build a StateAPI join the touches."
severity = "blocker"

